# Test: ze "-" means stdin (read) / stdout (write) across filename-accepting commands
# VALIDATES: migrated commands ACCEPT the "-" token and produce correct output.
# Design: plan/spec-cli-dash-stdio.md
#
# HARNESS NOTE (load-bearing): the .ci runner materializes a `stdin=` payload for
# a `ze <cmd> -` step into a TEMP FILE and rewrites the "-" arg to that path
# (internal/test/runner/runner_exec.go "ze reads config from file, not stdin"),
# rather than piping the process's real stdin. 700+ existing steps depend on this
# (`ze -`, `ze config validate -`, `ze bgp decode -`). So these steps prove the
# command ACCEPTS "-" and renders correctly (equivalent to the real-path case,
# AC-13); they do NOT exercise the literal stdin fd. The stdin-fd routing, the
# stdin-once guard (AC-9), and MRT magic-byte sniffing on stdin (AC-6) are proven
# by unit tests that inject stdin directly via cliio.SwapStreams:
#   internal/core/cliio/cliio_test.go, cmd_show_test.go (TestShowConfigDash),
#   cmd_import_test.go (TestImportSingleStdin/TestImportDoubleStdin).

stdin=cfg:terminator=EOF_CFG
bgp {
	router-id 1.2.3.4;
	session {
		asn {
			local 65000;
		}
	}
	peer edge1 {
		connection {
			local {
				ip 2.2.2.2;
			}
			remote {
				ip 1.1.1.1;
			}
		}
		session {
			asn {
				remote 65001;
			}
		}
	}
}
EOF_CFG

# --- Phase 1: config show - (the reported case, AC-1) ---
# Whole tree from stdin.
cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze config show -:stdin=cfg:exit=0
expect=stdout:contains=router-id 1.2.3.4
expect=stdout:contains=peer edge1
expect=stdout:contains=local 65000

# Path-scoped after "-" (AC-2): "-" does not disturb positional parsing.
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze config show - bgp peer edge1:stdin=cfg:exit=0
expect=stdout:contains=1.1.1.1
expect=stdout:contains=remote 65001
expect=stdout:not_contains=router-id 1.2.3.4

# --- Phase 2: migrated config/cli readers still accept "-" (AC-4) ---
# validate - (was an ad-hoc if path=="-" branch, now the shared helper).
cmd=foreground:seq=3:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=cfg:exit=0

# dump - (was a loadConfigData caller, now the shared helper).
cmd=foreground:seq=4:exec=ze config dump -:stdin=cfg:exit=0
expect=stdout:contains=router-id 1.2.3.4

# fmt - (was a loadConfigData caller, now the shared helper): reads the config and
# prints the reformatted tree to stdout.
cmd=foreground:seq=5:exec=ze config fmt -:stdin=cfg:exit=0
expect=stdout:contains=router-id 1.2.3.4

# The DATA spelling of the same pair, `show config dump -`, cannot be tested in
# this suite: `runExecCommands` (internal/test/runner/runner_exec.go) splits an
# exec line with strings.Fields, so the quotes around a `ze cli -c "..."` value
# reach the binary as literal characters and the command never matches a
# local-data handler (plan/journal/delegation-hands-the-callee-a-different-argv.md,
# 2026-08-31). It lives in test/parse/cli-config-dump-stdin.ci, whose suite uses
# the quote-aware splitCommand.

# The double-stdin guard (AC-9) and the literal stdin fd cannot be exercised here
# (see the HARNESS NOTE at the top of this file): the runner rewrites "-" to a temp
# file. They are proven by unit tests cmd_import_test.go (TestImportDoubleStdin) and
# cliio_test.go (TestStdinClaimedOnce).
